data: {"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Validated recipe — cctp@2\n_human-validated 2026-08-07 by farseen (github: FarseenSh)_\n_source: recipes/cctp/usdc-bridge-send.yaml_\n\n**Receipts** — what was actually run, on 2026-08-07, by farseen (github: FarseenSh)\n- checks: attest, test\n- chains exercised: base-sepolia, arbitrum-sepolia\n- on-chain:\n  - txHash: `0xd4b4e6395f52ad726dd6062e7a7ec47a2d3a7875d36f20fbb154cde756a3d0f5` — approve on base-sepolia\n  - txHash: `0xb0db8b585460b086c405ef4fd2a035e130b04b81729feb997235bcd6162421e6` — approve on base-sepolia\n  - txHash: `0xdba9da61c7873b092113dd2ad6a81b4104cd7d47264515ff0ae7aee2e11a0f74` — burn (depositForBurn) on base-sepolia\n  - txHash: `0xcd869bb6b169d29e9586380a90af688231b1fdbe9bc9db00e0081c53a7bd2dab` — mint (receiveMessage) on arbitrum-sepolia\n  - txHash: `0x14600541732355b12bf44d1370cbfdd14dd16bba42b14b5d79d7c87ad26c3080` — attestation probe on base-sepolia\n- gas: see `gas_notes` — the measured figures live there with their conditions, and a receipt that restated them without those conditions would be a number without its composition.\n- what these receipts do NOT prove: ⚠ ONE round trip is receipted — approve, burn on base-sepolia, mint on arbitrum-sepolia. The banner says `both tiers`; the SECOND tier's transaction hashes are NOT in the records. It was observed during validation and its hashes were not written down, which is a different thing from not having happened — and a receipts block must say which of the two it is.\n\n# Recipe: cctp @2 :: usdc-bridge-send\n# STATUS: ✅ VALIDATED 2026-08-07 (UTC) by farseen (github: FarseenSh) — THE TRANSFER COMPLETED: 1.000000 USDC burned on Base Sepolia, minted on Arbitrum Sepolia — both legs RECEIPTED (see `receipts.on_chain`, re-verified by RPC 2026-08-20). A second, finalized-tier transfer was observed during validation and its hashes were NOT recorded; the `both tiers` claim is therefore not receipted and is narrowed here rather than repeated. 9 mistakes · 47 quotes · 24/24 keyless. Stamp commit f646501. (Bookkeeping repair 2026-08-12: the fields and the stamp commit below were always the record; this banner had not been flipped. No new validation — session log.)\nproject_id: \"cctp\"          # the PUBLISHER name — never carries the major\nversion_major: 2            # the coexisting-majors key. v1 is LIVE; see v1_legacy_note.\nversion: \"2\"                # CCTP protocol major. Not an npm semver — this is a protocol.\ntype: \"usdc-bridge-send\"\n\n# chains on which this recipe has been CONCRETELY TESTED (05- §2.2). Not the target list.\n# What the validation transfer actually reached. Mainnet addresses are verified on-chain by read\n# calls (stage 0) but NO MAINNET TRANSFER HAS EVER RUN — deployments is not chains.\nchains:\n  - base-sepolia\n  - arbitrum-sepolia\n\n# ── deployments ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# EVERY address verified on-chain 2026-08-07 and cross-checked against the others:\n# TokenMessenger.localMessageTransmitter() → MessageTransmitter, TokenMessenger.localMinter() →\n# TokenMinter, TokenMinter.localTokenMessenger() → TokenMessenger (both ends of the relation),\n# and MessageTransmitter.localDomain() → the `domain` stated here. Re-asserted by stage 0 of the\n# shadow test on every run. Domains are READ FROM THE CONTRACT, not from a docs table.\ndeployments:\n  ethereum:\n    domain: 0\n    chain_id: 1\n    token_messenger_v2: \"0x28b5a0e9C621a5BadaA536219b3a228C8168cf5d\"\n    message_transmitter_v2: \"0x81D40F21F12A8F0E3252Bccb954D722d4c464B64\"\n    token_minter_v2: \"0xfd78EE919681417d192449715b2594ab58f5D002\"\n  base:\n    domain: 6\n    chain_id: 8453\n    token_messenger_v2: \"0x28b5a0e9C621a5BadaA536219b3a228C8168cf5d\"\n    message_transmitter_v2: \"0x81D40F21F12A8F0E3252Bccb954D722d4c464B64\"\n    token_minter_v2: \"0xfd78EE919681417d192449715b2594ab58f5D002\"\n  arbitrum:\n    domain: 3\n    chain_id: 42161\n    token_messenger_v2: \"0x28b5a0e9C621a5BadaA536219b3a228C8168cf5d\"\n    message_transmitter_v2: \"0x81D40F21F12A8F0E3252Bccb954D722d4c464B64\"\n    token_minter_v2: \"0xfd78EE919681417d192449715b2594ab58f5D002\"\n  base-sepolia:\n    domain: 6\n    chain_id: 84532\n    token_messenger_v2: \"0x8FE6B999Dc680CcFDD5Bf7EB0974218be2542DAA\"\n    message_transmitter_v2: \"0xE737e5cEBEEBa77EFE34D4aa090756590b1CE275\"\n    token_minter_v2: \"0xb43db544E2c27092c107639Ad201b3dEfAbcF192\"\n    usdc: \"0x036CbD53842c5426634e7929541eC2318f3dCF7e\"\n  arbitrum-sepolia:\n    domain: 3\n    chain_id: 421614\n    token_messenger_v2: \"0x8FE6B999Dc680CcFDD5Bf7EB0974218be2542DAA\"\n    message_transmitter_v2: \"0xE737e5cEBEEBa77EFE34D4aa090756590b1CE275\"\n    token_minter_v2: \"0xb43db544E2c27092c107639Ad201b3dEfAbcF192\"\n    usdc: \"0x75faf114eafb1BDbe2F0316DF893fd58CE46AA4d\"\n\n# ── working_example ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nworking_example:\n  code: |\n    // ── cctp-v2-bridge.ts ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n    // CCTP v2, Base Sepolia (domain 6) → Arbitrum Sepolia (domain 3).\n    // Signatures: circlefin/evm-cctp-contracts @ a92a2b4e, src/v2/  [C1][C7]\n    import {\n      createPublicClient, createWalletClient, http, pad, parseAbi, erc20Abi,\n    } from 'viem'\n    import { privateKeyToAccount } from 'viem/accounts'\n    import { arbitrumSepolia, baseSepolia } from 'viem/chains'\n\n    const SRC_DOMAIN = 6, DST_DOMAIN = 3\n    const TOKEN_MESSENGER      = '0x8FE6B999Dc680CcFDD5Bf7EB0974218be2542DAA'\n    const MESSAGE_TRANSMITTER  = '0xE737e5cEBEEBa77EFE34D4aa090756590b1CE275'\n    const TOKEN_MINTER         = '0xb43db544E2c27092c107639Ad201b3dEfAbcF192'\n    const SRC_USDC             = '0x036CbD53842c5426634e7929541eC2318f3dCF7e'\n    const IRIS                 = 'https://iris-api-sandbox.circle.com'\n\n    const FINALITY_CONFIRMED = 1000            // the v2 fast path  [C6] — FEE-GATED, see below\n\n    const tokenMessengerAbi = parseAbi([\n      'function depositForBurn(uint256 amount, uint32 destinationDomain, bytes32 mintRecipient, address burnToken, bytes32 destinationCaller, uint256 maxFee, uint32 minFinalityThreshold)',\n    ])\n    const transmitterAbi = parseAbi([\n      'function receiveMessage(bytes message, bytes attestation) returns (bool)',\n    ])\n    const minterAbi = parseAbi([\n      'function getLocalToken(uint32 remoteDomain, bytes32 remoteToken) view returns (address)',\n    ])\n\n\n_… recipe truncated for budget — 56012 bytes total, full text at the source path above._\n_Continue it: `web3_fetch` with `cursor: \"recipe:cctp@2::usdc-bridge-send::body@4839\"` — each call returns the next slice and the next cursor until there is none._\n\n**Citations** (preserved through truncation — degrade bodies, never citations):\n- https://iris-api-sandbox.circle.com\n- https://github.com/circlefin/evm-cctp-contracts/blob/a92a2b4e7e6ef99bf0b05dca71780f5ec190e729/src/v2/TokenMessengerV2.sol\n- https://github.com/circlefin/evm-cctp-contracts/blob/a92a2b4e7e6ef99bf0b05dca71780f5ec190e729/src/v2/TokenMessengerV2.sol#L166\n- https://github.com/tradingstrategy-ai/web3-ethereum-defi/pull/1099\n- https://github.com/circlefin/evm-cctp-contracts/issues/105\n- https://iris-api.circle.com/v2/messages/6?transactionHash=0x14600541…\n- https://github.com/circlefin/evm-cctp-contracts/issues/111\n- https://github.com/circlefin/evm-cctp-contracts/blob/a92a2b4e7e6ef99bf0b05dca71780f5ec190e729/src/v2/TokenMessengerV2.sol#L210\n- https://sepolia.base.org`.\n- https://iris-api.circle.com\n- https://developers.circle.com/cctp\n\n---\n\n### circle-fin-provider-cctp-v2@latest::index.d::ChainDefinitionWithCCTPv2\n`circle-fin-provider-cctp-v2@latest` · artifact:@circle-fin/provider-cctp-v2@1.11.0 · as_of 2026-08-20T23:25:41.820Z\nhttps://unpkg.com/@circle-fin/provider-cctp-v2@1.11.0/index.d.cts#L318-L355\n\n```\n/**\n* Chain definition with CCTPv2 configuration.\n* @alias ChainDefinitionWithCCTPv2\n*